+        /// Every entry moved into `new`. The groups the last two entries
+        /// went to, and the lanes they took, are kept: an entry homed to
+        /// one of them takes the lane after, and loads a spare group in
+        /// place of its own, so no entry loads a group a tag was just
+        /// stored into, a load the store would hold up (a 16-byte load over
+        /// a pending 1-byte store waits for it to commit). An entry whose
+        /// group is full is placed by `emplace`.
+        fn moveAll(self: *const Self, es: [*]Element, new: Arrays) void {
+            const spare: Group = .{ .m = @splat(0) };
+            var p1: usize = std.math.maxInt(usize);
+            var l1: usize = 0;
+            var p2: usize = std.math.maxInt(usize);
+            var l2: usize = 0;
+            for (0..self.mask + 1) |g| {
